// The TiDE app icon for the Windows standalone executable.
//
// Deliberately NOT part of SynthEdit.rc: that file is MFC-generated, not in
// the build, and resurrecting it for one icon would drag resource.h and the
// P9 drift question into the exe. This two-line file is the whole story.
//
// Resource id 1 on purpose -- Explorer shows the icon with the LOWEST id as
// the file's icon, so a bare numeric 1 cannot be out-ranked by anything a
// library contributes later.
//
// icons/TiDE.ico is COMMITTED, generated by scripts/render-icons.py from
// SynthEditSem/TiDE.icon (the single source of truth) -- the Windows CI
// runner has neither actool nor rsvg, so it cannot render this itself.
1 ICON "icons/TiDE.ico"
